Intermittent, timing-dependent failure only observed under the full concurrent test suite (not reproducible in isolation): z3-4.14.1 emits an undocumented multi-line diagnostic comment block (e.g. "; :zzz line: 2 position: 0" followed by a "; Suppported get-info parameters:" listing) on stdout immediately after each "unsupported" response to an unrecognized get-info parameter, which jSMTLIB's response parser normally strips as standard SMT-LIB ';' comments; under concurrent solver-process load a chunk of one of these comment blocks occasionally leaks into the raw text handed to the next command's response parser instead of being fully consumed with the first, producing an unparseable "Could not parse response from the solver for: ..." error and shifting the real response down by one slot -- the same solver-process stream-reading race also seen with z3-4.14.1 on ok_setOptionalOptions.tst and z3-4.8.12 on err_declareSortParameter_sortAfter.tst, not a defect in the test or golden
